__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pdf
*.zip
*.pptx
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.lnk
.DS_Store
tools/local/flywheel/router_decisions.jsonl
tools/selfimprove/proposals.jsonl
state/hook-fires.log

# Credentials. tools/lib/envload.py treats a repo-local .env as a valid override
# path, so one landing here must never be committable. new-recruit already ignores
# its own .env at .gitignore:12; this repo had no rule at all until 2026-07-25.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Per-API call ledger. Append-only and machine-local: it records timestamps and
# HTTP statuses, never key material, but it is local telemetry, not shared state.
state/api-usage.jsonl
state/openrouter-models.json

# Local safety nets and crash droppings, never shared state. The pre-edit copy of
# settings.json is kept on disk deliberately: the version it backs up (live Windows
# config before the ship-gate Stop hook) exists in no commit.
*.bak-pre-*
*.stackdump

# A2A read positions, one small integer per lane. state/bus.jsonl IS shared and IS
# tracked; how far one machine has read through it is not. Tracking these would
# conflict on every pull, and a fresh clone would start mid-stream and skip every
# message sent before the clone. Ignored deliberately, with one consequence
# accepted: a cursor's prior value is then unrecoverable, which is how lane B's
# pre-reset value was already lost on 2026-07-25.
state/bus-cursors/

# Mutation-harness scratch. tools/audit/mutate.py writes a mutated copy of a target
# BESIDE the original, because several targets resolve their repo root from
# __file__ and a copy under %TEMP% would get a root that does not exist, turning
# every case into a launch failure that then looks "caught". Removed in a finally
# block and swept at startup; ignored so a crash cannot commit one.
_mutant_*.py

# Mutation-run lock (tools/audit/mutate.py). A directory, created atomically with
# mkdir, holding the pid of the run that owns it. Two concurrent runs would
# overwrite each other's mutants and the verdicts would be meaningless.
.mutate-lock/
